3. THE VENDORED FILE
===============================================================================

  Vendored as:  data/math_500.jsonl  (500 records, one JSON object per line)
  Fetched from: https://huggingface.co/datasets/HuggingFaceH4/MATH-500
  Hub revision: 6e4ed1a2a79af7d8630a6b768ec859cb5af4d3be
  Upstream file: test.jsonl
  Upstream file SHA-256 (identical to the vendored copy):
    35dc41080a3680858b27fa7e0533d2d547825316fc5dafe5d316f4ccc5a06132

  The vendored file is a byte-identical copy of the upstream test.jsonl
  (Hash of the Hugging Face blob and of data/math_500.jsonl match). Fields in
  each record: problem, solution, answer, subject, level, unique_id — all
  preserved verbatim; nothing is rewritten, dropped or reordered.

  The pack uses two fields only: `problem` (the statement, sent verbatim) and
  `answer` (the published gold answer, compared textually after
  normalization). `solution`, `subject`, `level` and `unique_id` are used for
  integrity checks and the per-subject result breakdown; the full record stays
  in the vendored file so runs can be traced back to the exact bytes.

  The code in this repository is MIT licensed; the data is included under the
  upstream MIT terms above with attribution in NOTICE.
